                            <comment id="17178060" author="jason0h" created="Fri, 14 Aug 2020 21:03:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve tested out a fix, replacing line 597 of InterpreterSettingManager:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;return interpreterSetting.getDefaultInterpreterInfo().getEditor();&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With this:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;return interpreterSetting.getInterpreterInfo(intpName).getEditor();&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Gives me the correct behavior. I believe the previous line being set to always get the default interpreter is why the editor of the&#160; default interpreter would work correctly but none of the others would.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17178757" author="zjffdu" created="Mon, 17 Aug 2020 06:42:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue resolved by pull request 3877&lt;br/&gt;
